# PROJECT_SPEC.md §M7 packaging. Deny-by-default: exclude everything, then
# re-include only what the image build actually needs. A deny-by-default
# list can't have a "looks like it excludes a secret but doesn't match"
# entry for a file that doesn't exist yet -- the failure mode a blacklist
# invites -- because anything not explicitly re-included stays excluded
# regardless of what gets added to the repo later.
#
# tests/cassettes/ is deliberately NOT re-included: the image ships no
# cassettes, so `sul validate` in-container would silently fall back to
# FakeProvider (sul.cli._select_validate_provider) rather than replaying
# Config A. The container's job is the dashboard + `sul demo`, not
# `sul validate` -- see PROJECT_SPEC.md §M7's packaging note.
*

!src/
!src/**
!configs/
!configs/**
!artefacts/
!artefacts/**
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock

# Bytecode caches accumulate under src/ from local `pytest`/`mypy` runs and
# would otherwise ride along with the broad !src/** re-inclusion above --
# re-excluded here, after it, since Docker's own last-match-wins rule means
# order matters. Confirmed via a real `docker build` (COPY . /ctx) that
# these actually reach the build context without this: PROJECT_SPEC.md §M7's
# packaging deviation records the before/after file list.
**/__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/**
**/*.pyc
